{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_32h2mjxwmbynhu7qat7erplzqylzwd6mrckryv436j2tm74z6oka","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01TvnyiWE1eV81WdLQ2MFYyc","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-oXxm9Q/tmpwk/configs_raw.md","content":"| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [ ] |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | `js_newstate`, `js_freestate` | `js_newstate(NULL, NULL, 0)` — default allocator (`js_defaultalloc`), `actx=NULL`, `flags=0` so `J->strict==J->default_strict==0`; immediately `js_freestate`. Asserts `sizeof(js_Value)==16`. | [ ] |\n| 2 | `js_newstate`, `js_dostring` | `flags = JS_STRICT` (=1) so `J->strict=J->default_strict=1` (jsstate.c:204); then `js_dostring(J, \"x = 1;\")` → hits `jsrun.c:1132` `js_referenceerror(\"assignment to undeclared variable 'x'\")`, returns 1. | [ ] |\n| 3 | `js_newstate`, `js_dostring` | `flags = 0`; `js_dostring(J, \"x = 1; x\")` → `js_setvar` falls through to `jsR_setproperty(J->G,...)`, returns 0. Contrast row 2. | [ ] |\n| 4 | `js_newstate` | Out-of-band flag bits with JS_STRICT clear: `flags = 0xFFFFFFFE` / `flags = 2` / `flags = 0x80000000`. Only bit 0 is tested; state must be non-strict. Verify with `js_dostring(J,\"y=1\")` succeeding. | [ ] |\n| 5 | `js_newstate` | Out-of-band bits with JS_STRICT set: `flags = -1`, `flags = 0x7FFFFFFF`, `flags = 3`. All must behave identically to `flags=1`. | [ ] |\n| 6 | `js_newstate` with custom `js_Alloc` | Allocator that returns NULL for the very first request (`size == sizeof(js_State)`) → `js_newstate` returns NULL, nothing leaked. | [ ] |\n| 7 | `js_newstate` with custom `js_Alloc` | Allocator that succeeds for the state but returns NULL for the `JS_STACKSIZE * 16` stack allocation → `alloc(actx, J, 0)` then return NULL (jsstate.c:214-218). | [ ] |\n| 8 | `js_newstate` with custom `js_Alloc` + `actx` | Allocator that succeeds N times then fails, so the `js_try` at jsstate.c:224 fires inside `jsB_init` → `js_freestate(J)` and `js_newstate` returns NULL. Also verify `actx` pointer is passed through to every alloc call. | [ ] |\n| 9 | `js_setcontext`, `js_getcontext` | `js_getcontext` before any set → NULL (memset 0); `js_setcontext(J, &ctx)` then `js_getcontext` → `&ctx`; `js_setcontext(J, NULL)` back to NULL. | [ ] |\n| 10 | `js_setreport`, `js_report` | (a) default report (`js_defaultreport` → stderr); (b) `js_setreport(J, mycb)` then `js_report(J,\"msg\")` → callback receives exactly \"msg\"; (c) `js_setreport(J, NULL)` then `js_report` → no call (jsstate.c:168 `if (J->report)`). | [ ] |\n| 11 | `js_atpanic`, `js_throw` | `js_atpanic(J, mypanic)` returns previous (`js_defaultpanic`); then `js_pushstring(J,\"e\"); js_throw(J)` with `J->trytop==0` → `J->panic(J)` called, then `abort()`. Also `js_atpanic(J, NULL)` → `js_throw` aborts with no panic call. | [ ] |\n| 12 | `js_newstate(JS_STRICT)`, `js_ploadstring` | Strict-mode compile-time rejections, one source each: `\"with(o){}\"` (jscompile.c:1265), `\"delete x\"` (jscompile.c:507), `\"var implements\"`/`interface`/`package`/`private`/`protected`/`public`/`static`/`yield`/`let` (strictfuturewords, jscompile.c:44), `\"var arguments\"`, `\"var eval\"`, `\"function f(arguments){}\"`, `\"arguments = 1\"`, `\"eval = 1\"`, `\"try{}catch(eval){}\"`. Each → `js_ploadstring` returns 1 with SyntaxError. | [ ] |\n| 13 | `js_newstate(0)`, `js_ploadstring` | Same sources as row 12 in a NON-strict state → all must compile (return 0). | [ ] |\n| 14 | `js_newstate(0)`, `js_dostring` | Per-function `\"use strict\"` directive prologue (jscompile.c:1382-1385): `\"function f(){'use strict'; return this===undefined;} f()\"` → true, while enclosing script stays non-strict. Also `\"'use strict'; ...\"` at script top. | [ ] |\n| 15 | `js_newstate(JS_STRICT)` vs `js_newstate(0)`, `js_dostring` | `OP_THIS` branch (jsrun.c:1652): `\"function f(){return typeof this;} f()\"` → st