ringtonumber` branches: `\"0x1f\"`/`\"0X1F\"` hex, `\"0x\"` (s[2]==0 → falls through to float parse), `\"Infinity\"`, `\"+Infinity\"`, `\"-Infinity\"`, leading/trailing whitespace `\" 12 \"`, `\"\"` → 0, `\"12abc\"` → NaN, `\"1e3\"`/`\"1.5\"` (isflt → `js_strtod`), `\"-12\"`/`\"+12\"` (integer `js_strtol` path). | [ ] |\n| 115 | `js_dostring` `parseInt`/`parseFloat` | `parseInt` radix argument: absent (0 → auto-detect `0x` → 16, else 10), 2, 16, 36, 1 → NaN, 37 → NaN; leading `+`/`-`/whitespace; unparsable → NaN. `parseFloat(\"Infinity\")`, `parseFloat(\"-Infinity\")`, `parseFloat(\"abc\")` → NaN. | [ ] |\n| 116 | `js_gc` | `js_gc(J, 0)` — no report. Call immediately after `js_newstate`, then after allocating and dropping 100 objects; verify objects/strings/props are reclaimed and `J->gcthresh == remaining * JS_GCFACTOR`. | [ ] |\n| 117 | `js_gc`, `js_setreport` | `js_gc(J, 1)` — report path (jsgc.c:252): install a `js_Report` callback and assert the \"garbage collected (N%): ... envs, ... funs, ... objs, ... props, ... strs\" message shape. Also `js_gc(J,1)` with `J->report == NULL`. | [ ] |\n| 118 | `js_dostring` + automatic GC | Implicit `js_gc(J, 0)` from `jsR_run` when `J->gccounter > J->gcthresh` (jsrun.c:1608): allocation-heavy loop with the default `gcthresh=0` so the first iteration collects; confirms `JS_GCFACTOR` stabilisation over several cycles. | [ ] |\n| 119 | `js_ref`, `js_unref`, `js_getregistry` | Fixed-name branches (jsrun.c:942-956): `js_pushundefined` → `\"_Undefined\"`, `js_pushnull` → `\"_Null\"`, `js_pushboolean(1)` → `\"_True\"`, `js_pushboolean(0)` → `\"_False\"`. Two refs to the same primitive return the same name. `js_unref` then `js_getregistry` → undefined. | [ ] |\n| 120 | `js_ref` | Object branch: `js_newobject; js_ref` → interned `\"%p\"` string; ref'ing the SAME object twice gives the same name; two different objects give different names. GC must not collect the referenced object (reachable via `J->R`). | [ ] |\n| 121 | `js_ref` | C