nction calling `js_error`) → `js_tryrepr(J, -1, \"ERR\")` returns `\"ERR\"` and pops the exception; contrast `js_torepr` on the same value, which propagates. | [ ] |\n| 129 | `js_ploadstring` | Valid source `\"1+1\"` → returns 0 with a `JS_CSCRIPT` object on the stack (callable via `js_pushundefined; js_call(J,0)`). `filename` argument variants: `\"test.js\"` and `NULL`. | [ ] |\n| 130 | `js_ploadstring` | Syntax error source `\"function{\"` / `\"var\"` / unterminated string `\"'abc\"` / unterminated comment → returns 1 with a SyntaxError object on the stack; `jsP_freeparse` ran (no leak). Also `>JS_ASTLIMIT` (400) nested parens → \"too much recursion\". | [ ] |\n| 131 | `js_ploadstring` at the try limit | 64 nested `js_try` frames so `J->trytop == JS_TRYLIMIT`, then `js_ploadstring` → `js_ptry` pushes the literal `\"exception stack overflow\"` and returns 1 WITHOUT longjmp (jsstate.c:5-13, 36-45). | [ ] |\n| 132 | `js_pcall` | Success: `js_getglobal(\"Math\"); js_getproperty(-1,\"max\")` … or simpler `js_newcfunction` + `js_pushundefined` + args, `js_pcall(J, n)` for n = 0, 1, 3 → returns 0, result at top, stack trimmed to `savetop+1`. | [ ] |\n| 133 | `js_pcall` | Failure: callee throws (`js_newcfunction` whose body calls `js_typeerror`) → returns 1, stack holds exactly the error object at `savetop`. Also non-callable callee (`js_pushnumber` in the function slot) → returns 1 with \"number is not callable\". Also `js_pcall(J, -1)` → rangeerror \"number of arguments cannot be negative\". | [ ] |\n| 134 | `js_pconstruct` | Success with a script-defined constructor (generic path: reads `prototype`, creates `jsV_newobject`, returns the new object when the body returns a non-object) and with a body that returns an object (`js_rot2pop1` path, jsrun.c:1383-1387). n = 0 and n = 2. | [ ] |\n| 135 | `js_pconstruct` | Failure: constructor throws → returns 1 with only the error object; `prototype` property not an object → falls back to `J->Object_prototype`; non-callable target → returns 1. | [ ] |\n| 136 | `js_dostring` | Three outcomes: (a) `\"1+1\"` → 0; (b) runtime throw `\"throw new Error('boom')\"` → 1 AND `js_report` called with the `js_trystring(J,-1,\"Error\")` text; (c) syntax error `\"(\"` → 1 with the report; (d) at `trytop==JS_TRYLIMIT` → reports the literal \"exception stack overflow\" and returns 1. | [ ] |\n| 137 | `js_loadstring`, `js_eval`, `js_call` | Non-p variant: `js_try` around `js_loadstring(J,\"f.js\",\"(\")` → exception propagates to the caller's setjmp. Then the `iseval` flag difference (jsstate.c:122-124): `js_loadstring` compiles with `J->default_strict` and scope `J->GE`, whereas `js_eval` (→`js_loadeval`) compiles with `J->strict` and scope `J->strict ? J->E : NULL`. Test both with a state built with and without `JS_STRICT`, and `js_eval` with a NON-string on top (returns immediately, jsrun.c:1392). | [ ] |\n| 138 | `js_savetry`/`js_try`, `js_endtry`, `js_throw` | Manual protection: `if (js_try(J)) { /* handler */ }` … `js_endtry(J)`. Verify `E`, `envtop`, `tracetop`, `top`, `bot`, `strict` are all restored by `js_throw` (jsrun.c:1465-1478) by throwing from inside a nested call with a non-empty stack. | [ ] |\n| 139 | `js_endtry` | Underflow: `js_endtry(J)` with `J->trytop == 0` → `js_error(J,\"endtry: exception stack underflow\")`. | [ ] |\n| 140 | `js_savetry` / `js_try` | Overflow: 64 successful `js_try` frames, then a 65th → `js_trystackoverflow` pushes the literal \"exception stack overflow\" and throws (jsrun.c:1446-1447). | [ ] |\n| 141 | `js_pushnumber` ×JS_STACKSIZE | Value-stack overflow: push until `TOP + 1 >= JS_STACKSIZE` (4096) → `CHECKSTACK` → `js_stackoverflow` throws the literal \"stack overflow\". Also deep recursion in a script hitting `jsR_savescope`/`JS_ENVLIMIT` (1024) and `jsR_pushtrace` → \"call stack overflow\". | [ ] |\n| 142 | `js_pop` | `js_pop(J, 0)`, `js_pop(J, n)` for exactly `js_gettop()`, and `js_pop` past BOT → `TOP=BOT` then `js_error \"stack underflow!\"` (jsrun.c:406-409