 `js_gettop`, `js_pushglobal`, `js_currentfunction`, `js_currentfunctiondata` | At the top level (`BOT == 0`): `js_currentfunction` pushes undefined and `js_currentfunctiondata` returns NULL (jsrun.c:204-216). Inside a `js_newcfunctionx` call (`BOT > 0`): both return the function object / its `data`. Also `js_pushglobal` identity vs `js_getglobal` of a known global. | [ ] |\n| 152 | `js_compare` | String/string → `strcmp` (`\"a\"` vs `\"b\"`, equal strings, `\"\"`); number/number (`1` vs `2`, equal); NaN on either side → `*okay = 0`; mixed string/number → numeric coercion; objects with `valueOf` (JS_HNUMBER preference). | [ ] |\n| 153 | `js_equal` | Every branch of jsvalue.c:646-691: string/string (across shrstr/litstr/memstr), same-type undefined/null/number/boolean/object, `null`≡`undefined` both orders, number vs string both orders, boolean→number retry both orders, primitive vs object (`toPrimitive` retry) both orders, and a falling-through mismatch → 0. | [ ] |\n| 154 | `js_strictequal` | Same matrix as row 153 but no coercion: string/string across all three representations, differing types → 0, NaN vs NaN → 0, `-0` vs `0` → 1, same object → 1, distinct objects → 0. | [ ] |\n| 155 | `js_instanceof` | (a) non-callable right operand → TypeError \"instanceof: invalid operand\"; (b) non-object left operand → 0 with no prototype walk; (c) right operand whose `prototype` is not an object → TypeError; (d) true case via a 2-level prototype chain; (e) false case. | [ ] |\n| 156 | `js_typeof`, `js_type` | All 8 `js_Type` tags plus the object sub-cases: shrstr/litstr/memstr → `\"string\"`/`JS_ISSTRING`; undefined; null → `\"object\"`/`JS_ISNULL`; boolean; number; `JS_CFUNCTION` and `JS_CCFUNCTION` objects → `\"function\"`/`JS_ISFUNCTION`; `JS_CSCRIPT` object → `\"object\"`/`JS_ISOBJECT` (note the asymmetry with `js_iscallable`); plain object; out-of-range idx → undefined. | [ ] |\n| 157 | `js_isdefined`, `js_isundefined`, `js_isnull`, `js_isboolean`, `js_isnumber`, `js_is