{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01F9MUfr2qSjtZPWWE8qXAGD","type":"tool_result","content":"//! Phase B — differential tests driving the raw C API (the lowest-level public\n//! entry points) through both `.so` files: state/flags, stack manipulation,\n//! push/new constructors, properties + attribute flags, arrays (flat/sparse),\n//! iterators, userdata, cfunctions, operators, repr, gc/dumpstrings.\n#![allow(non_snake_case)]\n\nmod common;\nuse common::*;\nuse std::ffi::{c_char, c_int, c_void};\n\nconst SEED: u64 = 0xC0FFEE_1234_5678;\n\n/* All state flag shapes the C actually distinguishes (only bit 0 is read). */\nconst FLAGSETS: [c_int; 6] = [0, JS_STRICT, 2, 3, -1, 0x7fffffff];\n\n/// `js_pushliteral` does NOT copy: the pointer must outlive the state, so it\n/// has to be a static string (a temporary CString would be a dangling read).\nfn lit_literal() -> *const c_char {\n    b\"literal\\0\".as_ptr() as *const c_char\n}\nfn lit_lit() -> *const c_char {\n    b\"lit\\0\".as_ptr() as *const c_char\n}\n\nfn dump(a: &Api, J: JS) {\n    unsafe {\n        let n = (a.js_gettop)(J);\n        emit(&format!(\"top={}\", n));\n        let e = cs(\"<repr!>\");\n        for i in 0..n {\n            emit(&format!(\"[{}]={}\", i, repr_at(a, J, i)));\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n/* push a fixed, varied set of values on the stack */\nfn push_zoo(a: &Api, J: JS) {\n    unsafe {\n        (a.js_pushundefined)(J);\n        (a.js_pushnull)(J);\n        (a.js_pushboolean)(J, 0);\n        (a.js_pushboolean)(J, 1);\n        (a.js_pushboolean)(J, 42);\n        (a.js_pushnumber)(J, 0.0);\n        (a.js_pushnumber)(J, -0.0);\n        (a.js_pushnumber)(J, f64::NAN);\n        (a.js_pushnumber)(J, f64::INFINITY);\n        (a.js_pushnumber)(J, -1.5);\n        (a.js_pushnumber)(J, 1e21);\n        (a.js_pushnumber)(J, 2147483647.0);\n        (a.js_pushstring)(J, cs(\"\").as_ptr());\n        (a.js_pushstring)(J, cs(\"short\").as_ptr());\n        (a.js_pushstring)(J, cs(\"123456789012345\").as_ptr()); /* 15 == shrstr max */\n        (a.js_pushstring)(J, cs(\"1234567890123456\").as_ptr()); /* 16 == memstr */\n        (a.js_pushliteral)(J, lit_literal());\n        (a.js_pushlstring)(J, cs(\"abcdef\").as_ptr(), 3);\n        (a.js_pushstring)(J, cs(\"\\u{e9}\\u{4e2d}\\u{1f600}\").as_ptr());\n        (a.js_newobject)(J);\n        (a.js_newarray)(J);\n        (a.js_newboolean)(J, 1);\n        (a.js_newnumber)(J, 7.25);\n        (a.js_newstring)(J, cs(\"boxed\").as_ptr());\n        (a.js_newregexp)(J, cs(\"a+b\").as_ptr(), JS_REGEXP_G);\n        (a.js_pushglobal)(J);\n        (a.js_newobjectx)(J);\n    }\n}\n\n/* ------------------------------------------------------- state / context */\n\n#[test]\nfn state_flags_context_atpanic_report() {\n    unsafe extern \"C\" fn rep(_J: JS, msg: *const c_char) {\n        emit(&format!(\"report:{}\", unsafe { rs(msg) }));\n    }\n    unsafe extern \"C\" fn pan(_J: JS) {\n        emit(\"panic\");\n    }\n    fn act(a: &Api, J: JS) {\n        unsafe {\n            (a.js_setcontext)(J, 0x1234 as *mut c_void);\n            emit(&format!(\"ctx={:?}\", (a.js_getcontext)(J)));\n            (a.js_setreport)(J, Some(rep));\n            (a.js_report)(J, cs(\"hello report\").as_ptr());\n            let old = (a.js_atpanic)(J, Some(pan));\n            emit(&format!(\"oldpanic_is_none={}\", old.is_none()));\n            let old2 = (a.js_atpanic)(J, old);\n            emit(&format!(\"restored={}\", old2 == Some(pan as unsafe extern \"C\" fn(JS))));\n            (a.js_pushnumber)(J, 1.0);\n        }\n=== \n1563 tests/phase_b_api.rs\n../c_src/build/libmujs.so\ntarget/release/libmujs.so","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_012gQ5jbjZW4mxgkHJC7hDEY","session_id":"2be16944-0c16-4bac-97a9-ffb5f1a29386","uuid":"a3617211-b249-493b-ac99-4ea9740b6191","timestamp":"2026-09-04T05:00:51.826Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Phase C builtins error tests"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_dgxy72nmz5g77r6yswwrtypx4bcbllhhofrowlhi76dtubkrt4va","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_013BFJZHq4ZNujDAFpdgcLtk","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Phase C regexp/utf/dtoa tests","run_in_background":false,"prompt":"You are writing DIFFERENTIAL tests for a C→Rust translation of MuJS.\n\nWorking dir: /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-oXxm9Q\n- `c_src/` = original C (ground truth, NEVER modify, never rebuild)\n- `translation/` = Rust crate under test. Run all cargo commands from `translation/`.\n\nYOUR TASK: create exactly ONE new file, `translation/tests/phase_c_regexp.rs`, with\ndifferential error-path tests for rows 500..593 of `translation/ERRORS.md`\n(jsregexp.c, regexp.c, utf.c, jsdtoa.c). Read those rows first.\n`translation/tests/phase_b_lowlevel.rs` already fuzzes regcomp/regexec/chartorune/\nstrtod on VALID inputs — your job is the explicit REJECTION rows: every distinct\n`die()` message, every limit, every throw.\n\nSTRICT RULES\n- Create ONLY `translation/tests/phase_c_regexp.rs`. Do NOT modify anything else:\n  not c_src/, not translation/src/, not tests/common/mod.rs, not other test files.\n- Never call Rust functions directly — only the two `.so` exports, via the harness.\n\nHARNESS (read `translation/tests/common/mod.rs`, `translation/tests/phase_b_lowlevel.rs`\nand `translation/tests/phase_b_api.rs` for working examples). Start your file with:\n    #![allow(non_snake_case)]\n    mod common;\n    use common::*;\nAvailable:\n- `Api` fields for every exported symbol, notably `js_regcomp(pattern, cflags,\n  &mut errorp) -> Prog`, `js_regexec(prog, string, &mut Resub, eflags)`,\n  `js_regfree`, `js_regcompx`/`js_regfreex` (explicit allocator), `jsU_chartorune`,\n  `jsU_runetochar`, `jsU_runelen`, `jsU_tolowerrune_full`, `js_strtod`, `js_strtol`,\n  `js_stringtofloat`, `js_grisu2`, `js_fmtexp`, `js_itoa`.\n- `Resub::default()` plus `REG_ICASE / REG_NEWLINE / REG_NOTBOL / REG_MAXSUB`.\n- `diff_eval(label, src, flags)` for the JS level (`new RegExp(...)`,\n  `String.prototype.match/replace/search/split`, `re.exec/test`, `re.lastIndex`).\n- `diff_native(label, act, flags)` + `emit()` + `set_pi/pi/pic`, `set_ps/ps` for the\n  raw C API inside a js_pcall (so throws are caught, never fatal).\n- `repr_at(a, J, idx)` / `str_at(a, J, idx)` for NON-destructive observation.\n- `Rng::new(seed)`, `same()`, `libs()`.\n\nTEST CONTENT — cover EVERY row 500..593:\n- Each of the ~21 distinct `die()` strings in regexp.c, driven through BOTH\n  `js_regcomp` (assert identical NULL result AND identical error string) and\n  `new RegExp(...)` at the JS level (assert identical SyntaxError text):\n  invalid escape sequence / invalid quantifier / unterminated escape sequence /\n  invalid escape character / numeric overflow / too many character classes /\n  invalid character class range / too many character class ranges /\n  unterminated character class / infinite loop matching the empty string /\n  invalid back-reference / too many captures / unmatched '(' / unmatched ')' /\n  syntax error / stack overflow / program too large.\n- The limit rows: REG_MAXSUB/too many captures (build a pattern with 17+ groups),\n  MAXPROG/\"program too large\" and MAXREP/\"numeric overflow\" (build with\n  programmatic repetition, e.g. `\"a{100}\"` nested or `x{2147483647}`), the\n  REG_MAXREC=4096 recursion limit in `match()` (a pattern+subject that recurses\n  deeply, e.g. `(a|aa)+$` against a long \"aaaa...\" string) — assert the two\n  libraries return the SAME return code (-1) and not merely \"both failed\".\n- jsregexp.c throws: `js_newregexp` with a bad pattern, out-of-range and negative\n  flag ints (8, 255, -1) passed across the FFI boundary, `new RegExp(re, 'g')`\n  (\"cannot supply flags when creating one RegExp from another\"), invalid flag\n  letters and duplicated flags, `js_toregexp` on a non-regexp (\"not a regexp\"),\n  `RegExp.prototype.exec/test` called on a non-regexp `this`, `lastIndex` beyond the\n  subject length, \"regexec failed\".\n- utf.c rejection rows: every `goto bad` path of `chartorune` (truncated sequences,\n  invalid continuation bytes, lead bytes >= 0xF8, the overlong `C0 80` case),\n  `runetochar` with c > Runemax and with negative c, `tolowerrune_full` /\n  `toupperrune_full` returning NULL, and `ucd_bsearch` misses. Compare the decoded\n  rune AND the returned length, for hand-picked byte sequences and for a few\n  thousand random byte strings with a fixed seed.\n- jsdtoa.c rows: the six explicit `js_strtod` guards (a second `.`, mantissa longer\n  than 18 digits, empty mantissa, exponent overflow both directions) — compare the\n  returned double BITS and the end-pointer offset. Include the `errno = ERANGE`\n  clamping cases (`1e999`, `1e-999`).\n\nDo NOT drive an error out of a `js_pcall` (that aborts the process). Do NOT use\n`diff_isolated`/`isolated_child`.\n\nWORKFLOW\n1. Write the file.\n2. `cd translation && timeout 600 cargo test --release --offline --test phase_c_regexp -- --test-threads=1`\n   (always `--offline`).\n3. Iterate until it compiles and runs.\n4. If a test reveals a GENUINE divergence between the C and Rust `.so`, do NOT touch\n   translation/src — mark it `#[ignore = \"DIVERGENCE: ...\"]` with a precise comment\n   and continue. The file must end with all non-ignored tests PASSING.\n5. Write covered row numbers to `tmpwk/covered_regexp.txt` (`<row> <test fn>`).\n\nFINAL REPORT: number of test fns, rows covered, and FULL detail of every divergence\nfound (exact input, C output, Rust output)."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":410,"cache_read_input_tokens":213318,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":410,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_i