{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_dgxy72nmz5g77r6yswwrtypx4bcbllhhofrowlhi76dtubkrt4va","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01UrTSzcsB8tDakT2p1ypBEu","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Phase B script-level config tests","run_in_background":false,"prompt":"You are writing DIFFERENTIAL tests for a C→Rust translation of MuJS.\n\nWorking dir: /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-oXxm9Q\n- `c_src/` = original C (ground truth, NEVER modify, never rebuild)\n- `translation/` = Rust crate under test. Run all cargo commands from `translation/`.\n\nYOUR TASK: create exactly ONE new file, `translation/tests/phase_b_script.rs`, with\nVALID-PATH (Phase B) differential tests for the JS-language / builtin-library rows of\n`translation/CONFIGS.md` — specifically the rows about: strings (shrstr ≤15 vs\nmemstr ≥16 vs literal, UTF-8 1/2/3/4 byte, js_utflen/js_runeat, reprstr vs fmtstr\nescaping), numbers (integer fast path, -0, NaN/Inf, all four jsV_numbertostring\nbranches, radix 2..36, toFixed/toExponential 0..20, toPrecision 1..21), arrays\n(flat vs sparse, empty/one/many, unflatten triggers), objects/prototypes/accessors,\nDate (all getters/setters, local timezone), JSON (stringify with replacer + every\nindent shape, parse round trips), RegExp (all 8 flag combinations, exec/test/match/\nreplace/split with and without /g and /m and /i), Math, Function.apply/call/bind,\nclosures/control flow, and getters/setters. Read CONFIGS.md first and cover the rows\nthat are driven from JS source rather than the raw C API (the raw-API rows are\nalready covered by `tests/phase_b_api.rs` and `tests/phase_b_lowlevel.rs` — read\nthose two files so you do not duplicate them).\n\nSTRICT RULES\n- Create ONLY `translation/tests/phase_b_script.rs`. Do NOT modify anything else:\n  not c_src/, not translation/src/, not tests/common/mod.rs, not other test files.\n- Never call Rust functions directly — only the two `.so` exports, via the harness.\n\nHARNESS (read `translation/tests/common/mod.rs` for the full list). Start with:\n    #![allow(non_snake_case)]\n    mod common;\n    use common::*;\nAvailable:\n- `diff_eval(label, src, flags)` — runs `src` in BOTH libraries and compares the\n  rendering `\"load-error(rc) msg\"` / `\"throw(rc) msg\"` / `\"ok <repr>\"` byte for byte.\n  `flags` is 0 or `JS_STRICT`. This is your main tool.\n- `diff_native(label, act, flags)`, `emit()`, `set_pi/pi/pic`, `set_ps/ps`,\n  `set_pf/pf` when you need the raw API.\n- `repr_at(a, J, idx)` / `str_at(a, J, idx)` for NON-destructive observation.\n- `Rng::new(seed)` with `.below/.range_i64/.f64/.string` for reproducible randomized\n  inputs; `same()`, `libs()`, `capture_stdout()`, `mask_ptrs()`.\n\nREQUIREMENTS\n- PROPERTY-STYLE: for every area, do not stop at one hand-picked value. Generate\n  MANY randomized inputs from a FIXED seed and format them into the JS source, e.g.\n  a few thousand random doubles through `String(x)`, `x.toFixed(k)`,\n  `x.toString(radix)`, `JSON.stringify(x)`, `parseFloat/parseInt`; random strings\n  through the full String method surface; random arrays through sort/join/slice/\n  splice/indexOf/concat/reverse; random dates through every Date getter.\n- Escape the generated values into the JS source carefully (or push them with the\n  raw API) so that the SAME bytes reach both libraries.\n- Run each area under both `flags = 0` and `flags = JS_STRICT`.\n- Keep the total runtime under about 3 minutes: prefer many small evals batched into\n  one script (build a script that loops over an array of inputs and joins the\n  results into one string) over one eval per input.\n\nDo NOT drive an error out of a `js_pcall` (that aborts the process): `diff_eval` and\n`diff_native` are always safe. Do NOT use `diff_isolated`/`isolated_child`.\n\nWORKFLOW\n1. Write the file.\n2. `cd translation && timeout 600 cargo test --release --offline --test phase_b_script -- --test-threads=1`\n   (always `--offline`).\n3. Iterate until it compiles and runs.\n4. If a test reveals a GENUINE divergence between the C and Rust `.so`, do NOT touch\n   translation/src — mark that test `#[ignore = \"DIVERGENCE: ...\"]` with a precise\n   comment and continue. The file must end with all non-ignored tests PASSING.\n5. Write the CONFIGS.md row numbers you covered to `tmpwk/covered_script.txt`\n   (`<row> <test fn>`).\n\nFINAL REPORT: number of test fns, CONFIGS.md rows covered, and FULL detail of every\ndivergence found (exact JS source, C output, Rust output)."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":410,"cache_read_input_tokens":213318,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":410,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2be16944-0c16-4bac-97a9-ffb5f1a29386","uuid":"7c0e3e26-6ce8-42c4-a89b-80c41e2ea47a","timestamp":"2026-09-04T05:01:15.075Z"}
