nslation/ERRORS.md`\n(jsobject.c, jsarray.c, jsfunction.c, jsboolean.c, jsnumber.c, jsstring.c, jsdate.c,\njsmath.c, json.c, jsbuiltin.c, jsrepr.c). Read those rows first.\n\nSTRICT RULES\n- Create ONLY `translation/tests/phase_c_builtins.rs`. Do NOT modify anything else:\n  not c_src/, not translation/src/, not tests/common/mod.rs, not other test files.\n- Never call Rust functions directly — only the two `.so` exports, via the harness.\n\nHARNESS (read `translation/tests/common/mod.rs` and `translation/tests/phase_b_api.rs`\nfor working examples). Start your file with:\n    #![allow(non_snake_case)]\n    mod common;\n    use common::*;\nAvailable:\n- `diff_eval(label, src, flags)` — runs JS source in BOTH libraries and compares the\n  rendering `\"load-error(rc) msg\"` / `\"throw(rc) msg\"` / `\"ok <repr>\"` byte for byte.\n  This is the natural tool for almost every row here: e.g.\n  `diff_eval(\"toFixed\", \"(5).toFixed(101)\", 0)`.\n- `diff_native(label, act, flags)` with `act: fn(&Api, JS)` for raw-API rows,\n  `emit()` for observations, `set_pi/pi/pic`, `set_ps/ps`, `set_pf/pf` for params.\n- `repr_at(a, J, idx)` / `str_at(a, J, idx)` for NON-destructive observation.\n- `Api` has a field per exported symbol; `libs()`, `same()`, `Rng`, `capture_stdout`.\n\nTEST CONTENT — cover EVERY row 339..499, one test fn per builtin area:\n- Object: Object.defineProperty/defineProperties/create/getOwnPropertyDescriptor/\n  keys/seal/freeze/preventExtensions/getPrototypeOf with non-object arguments,\n  invalid descriptors (both value and get/set), accessors that are not callable,\n  redefining non-configurable properties, `Object.prototype.toString.call` on every\n  primitive, `hasOwnProperty`/`isPrototypeOf`/`propertyIsEnumerable` on primitives.\n- Array: Array(len) with invalid lengths (-1, 1.5, NaN, 2^32, 1<<27), `length`\n  assignment errors, every Array.prototype method called on a non-object /\n  undefined `this`, `sort` with a non-callable comparator, `reduce` of an empty\n  array with no initial value, `join`/`concat` with cyclic arrays,\n  `forEach/map/filter/every/some/reduce/reduceRight` with non-callable callbacks.\n- Function: `Function.prototype.apply/call/bind` on non-functions, `apply` with a\n  non-array-like argument, `new Function('bad syntax')`, arity/`length`/`name`,\n  `Function.prototype.toString` on a bound/native function.\n- Boolean/Number/String prototype methods invoked on the wrong `this` type\n  (\"not a boolean\"/\"not a number\"/\"not a string\").\n- Number: toFixed/toExponential (digit range 0..20 → RangeError at -1 and 21),\n  toPrecision (1..21 → RangeError at 0 and 22), toString radix (2..36 → RangeError\n  at 1 and 37, plus fractional and NaN radixes).\n- String: fromCharCode with out-of-range and NaN codes, charAt/charCodeAt/indexOf/\n  slice/substring/substr/split/replace/match/search with NaN, ±Infinity and huge\n  indices, `replace` with a non-callable second argument, malformed surrogate input.\n- Date: new Date with 0..7 arguments and invalid values, Date.parse of malformed\n  strings, setFullYear/setMonth/... with NaN, toISOString on an invalid date\n  (RangeError), Date.prototype methods invoked on a non-Date `this`.\n- Math: every function with 0 arguments, NaN, ±Infinity, and wrong types;\n  Math.max/min with no arguments.\n- JSON: JSON.parse of every malformed input (`\"\"`, `\"{\"`, `\"[1\"`, `\"{'a':1}\"`,\n  trailing commas, bad escapes, bad numbers, deep-but-legal nesting), JSON.stringify\n  of cyclic structures (\"cyclic object value\"), of functions/undefined, with\n  replacer functions and arrays, and with every `space` shape (number, string, huge).\n- jsbuiltin.c: encodeURI/decodeURI/encodeURIComponent/decodeURIComponent with\n  malformed percent escapes and lone surrogates (URIError), parseInt/parseFloat with\n  odd radixes and junk, `eval` with non-string arguments.\n- jsrepr.c: js_repr/js_torepr/js_tryrepr on cyclic and deeply nested structures.\n- For every group ALSO add randomized coverage with a fixed seed: generate many\n  random argument values (use `Rng::f64()` and `Rng::string()`) for the numeric and\n  string methods and assert both libraries agree; this catches value-dependent bugs\n  a single hand-picked argument misses.\n- Run every source under both `flags = 0` and `flags = JS_STRICT`.\n\nDo NOT drive an error out of a `js_pcall` (that aborts the process): use\n`diff_eval`/`diff_native` only. Do NOT use `diff_isolated`/`isolated_child`.\n\nWORKFLOW\n1. Write the file.\n2. `cd translation && timeout 600 cargo test --release --offline --test phase_c_builtins -- --test-threads=1`\n   (always `--offline`).\n3. Iterate until it compiles and runs.\n4. If a test reveals a GENUINE divergence between the C and Rust `.so`, do NOT touch\n   translation/src — mark that test `#[ignore = \"DIVERGENCE: ...\"]` with a precise\n   comment and continue. The file must end with all non-ignored tests PASSING.\n5. Write covered row numbers to `tmpwk/covered_builtins.txt` (`<row> <test fn>`).\n\nFINAL REPORT: number of test fns, rows covered, and FULL detail of every divergence\nfound (exact JS source, C output, Rust output).","agentId":"ad441bc55241c7f06","agentType":"general-purpose","harnessNoteCount":0,"harnessTailCount":0,"harnessSectionHash":"a12b34dc24aa0b1f","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done.\n\n## Result\n\nCreated exactly one new file: `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-oXxm9Q/translation/tests/phase_c_builtins.rs` (81 KB). Nothing else in the repo was modified (`phase_c_regexp.rs` / `phase_c_syntax.rs` in that directory are other agents' files, not mine). Coverage map written to `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-oXxm9Q/tmpwk/covered_builtins.txt`.\n\n**23 test functions, all passing, 0 ignored, ~21.6 s wall time:**\n\n| test fn | ERRORS.md rows |\n|---|---|\n| `object_statics_on_non_objects` | 339-341, 344-345, 347-348, 350-356 |\n| `object_descriptors_and_accessors` | 342-343, 346, 349 |\n| `object_pro