{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"ab2546e23670cb062","tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_013BFJZHq4ZNujDAFpdgcLtk","status":"completed","output_file":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-agent-jBvmJB/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-work-oXxm9Q/2be16944-0c16-4bac-97a9-ffb5f1a29386/tasks/ab2546e23670cb062.output","summary":"Done. All tests pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nCreated **only** `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-oXxm9Q/translation/tests/phase_c_regexp.rs` (73 KB, **42 `#[test]` fns**: 41 passing + 1 `#[ignore]`d divergence record). Coverage map written to `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-oXxm9Q/tmpwk/covered_regexp.txt` (94 lines — every row 500…593).\n\n```\ncargo test --release --offline --test phase_c_regexp -- --test-threads=1\ntest result: ok. 41 passed; 0 failed; 1 ignored\n```\n\nNothing else was modified (`translation/src/`, `c_src/`, `tests/common/mod.rs` and all other test files untouched).\n\n### What is covered\n- **All 21 distinct `die()` strings in regexp.c**, each driven through *both* `js_regcomp` (identical NULL + identical error string, asserted against the expected C message for all 4 cflag combinations) *and* `new RegExp(...)` (identical `SyntaxError: regular expression: <msg>`). Boundary cases pinned on the accepting side too (`a{254}`, 128 classes, 31 spans, 15 captures, 4000 atoms).\n- **Limits**: `REG_MAXSUB` (16/17/20/40 groups + 17 nested), `MAXPROG` all three sites (`(?:a{254}){254}`, 16385-byte pattern, `\"a{99}\"×400`), `MAXREP` (`a{255}`, `a{1,255}`, `x{2147483647}`), `REG_MAXREC` in `count()` (4100/5000/8000 atoms, 4100 alternations) and in `match()` — asserting the C rc is exactly **-1**, not merely \"both failed\".\n- **Allocator failure rows 524/526/530/531** driven deterministically via `js_regcompx` with a counting allocator that fails on the Nth allocation, asserting each of the four distinct \"cannot allocate …\" messages plus the allocation count.\n- **Rows 533–549**: a 17-entry table (row → pattern/cflags/subject/eflags) asserting rc==1 in C and identical rc + capture offsets in both, plus the `sub==NULL` scratch path, extra newline runes (0xA/0xD/U+2028/U+2029) and the JS-level equivalents.\n- **jsregexp.c**: `js_newregexp` with 11 bad patterns × 4 flag words inside `js_pcall`; flag ints 8/9/255/-1/-2/`INT_MIN`/`0x7fffffff` across the FFI; `new RegExp(re,'g')`; all invalid/duplicated flag letters incl. `ToString`-converted flags; `js_toregexp` on 12 JS receivers × 3 methods and on 10 raw-API values; `lastIndex` beyond length; `regexec failed` from `exec`/`test`/`match`/`replace`/`search`/`split`. Rows 554/555/565 (`js_malloc` OOM) forced via `js_setlimit`'s memory limit with the limit restored after the caught throw.\n- **utf.c**: all 10 `goto bad` paths as a row-tagged table with asserted `len=1 rune=0xfffd`, every lead byte 0xF8–0xFF, every stray continuation 0x80–0xBF, `C0 80` → `len=2 rune=0x0`, plus 5000 random byte strings (fixed seed) walked rune-by-rune comparing length *and* rune; `runetochar` for `>Runemax`, negative and 0 with asserted byte sequences + `runelen`; `ucd_bsearch` misses over 5000 codepoints; `tolowerrune_full`/`toupperrune_full` swept over the whole BMP comparing NULL-ness and the mapping sequence.\n- **jsdtoa.c**: all six `js_strtod` guards comparing the returned **double bits** and the **end-pointer offset** (plus `NULL` endptr and `js_stringtofloat`), and the ERANGE clamps `1e999`/`1e-999` with a sweep of every decade around ±511. Rows 586/587 (the two `minus()` asserts — the C build has no `NDEBUG`, so they would `abort()`) covered as invariant checks over 4000 denormals, all 2046 exact powers of two, the largest finites and 20000 random finite doubles.\n\n### Divergence found (1)\n\n`#[ignore = \"DIVERGENCE: ...\"]` on `regexp_lastindex_out_of_ushort_range_DIVERGENCE`.\n\n**Root cause**: `js_Regexp.last` is `unsigned short` in both. C `jsrun.c:750` does `obj->u.r.last = jsV_tointeger(J, value);` — a C `double`→`unsigned short` conversion, which gcc implements as truncate-then-wrap modulo 65536. `translation/src/jsrun.rs:911` writes `(*obj).u.r.last = jsV_tointeger(J, value) as c_ushort;` and Rust's float→int `as` cast **saturates**.\n\n8 of 14 probed cases diverge (exact inputs / C / Rust):\n\n| input | C | Rust |\n|---|---|---|\n| `var r=/a/g; r.lastIndex=-1; [String(r.exec('aaa')), r.lastIndex].join(',')` | `\"null,0\"` | `\"a,1\"` |\n| `var r=/a/g; r.lastIndex=-1; [r.test('aaa'), r.lastIndex].join(',')` | `\"false,0\"` | `\"true,1\"` |\n| `var r=/a/g; r.lastIndex=-1; r.lastIndex` | `65535` | `0` |\n| `var r=/a/g; r.lastIndex=-100; r.lastIndex` | `65436` | `0` |\n| `var r=/a/g; r.lastIndex=65536; [String(r.exec('aaa')), r.lastIndex].join(',')` | `\"a,1\"` | `\"null,0\"` |\n| `var r=/a/g; r.lastIndex=65536; r.lastIndex` | `0` | `65535` |\n| `var r=/a/g; r.lastIndex=65537; r.lastIndex` | `1` | `65535` |\n| `var r=/a/g; r.lastIndex=131072; r.lastIndex` | `0` | `65535` |\n\n(`1e10`, `-1e10`, `Infinity`, `-Infinity` happen to agree and stay in the passing test.)\n\n### Notable C quirk pinned (both libraries agree, so not a divergence)\n`lexclass` tests escaped class members with `strchr(\"DSWdsw\", g->yychar)`, which truncates the rune to a `char`: `U+2000` (low byte 0x00) matches the terminating NUL and `U+2044` (low byte `'D'`) matches `'D'`. Such members are silently swallowed / expanded to `\\D` instead of becoming plain ranges, so e.g. `[\\u2000-\\u0001]` does **not** raise \"invalid character class range\". This forced the row-511 span generator to use base `0x2001` step 4 (low byte ≡ 1 mod 4 avoids 0x00 and all of `DSWdsw`); the quirk itself is now asserted identical in both libraries.","usage":{"total_tokens":203074,"tool_uses":75,"duration_ms":1231145},"uuid":"2d3e995e-90e0-4666-9168-02c9561fe312","session_id":"2be16944-0c16-4bac-97a9-ffb5f1a29386"}
