d Rust's float→int `as` cast **saturates**.\n\n8 of 14 probed cases diverge (exact inputs / C / Rust):\n\n| input | C | Rust |\n|---|---|---|\n| `var r=/a/g; r.lastIndex=-1; [String(r.exec('aaa')), r.lastIndex].join(',')` | `\"null,0\"` | `\"a,1\"` |\n| `var r=/a/g; r.lastIndex=-1; [r.test('aaa'), r.lastIndex].join(',')` | `\"false,0\"` | `\"true,1\"` |\n| `var r=/a/g; r.lastIndex=-1; r.lastIndex` | `65535` | `0` |\n| `var r=/a/g; r.lastIndex=-100; r.lastIndex` | `65436` | `0` |\n| `var r=/a/g; r.lastIndex=65536; [String(r.exec('aaa')), r.lastIndex].join(',')` | `\"a,1\"` | `\"null,0\"` |\n| `var r=/a/g; r.lastIndex=65536; r.lastIndex` | `0` | `65535` |\n| `var r=/a/g; r.lastIndex=65537; r.lastIndex` | `1` | `65535` |\n| `var r=/a/g; r.lastIndex=131072; r.lastIndex` | `0` | `65535` |\n\n(`1e10`, `-1e10`, `Infinity`, `-Infinity` happen to agree and stay in the passing test.)\n\n### Notable C quirk pinned (both libraries agree, so not a divergence)\n`lexclass` tests escaped class members with `strchr(\"DSWdsw\", g->yychar)`, which truncates the rune to a `char`: `U+2000` (low byte 0x00) matches the terminating NUL and `U+2044` (low byte `'D'`) matches `'D'`. Such members are silently swallowed / expanded to `\\D` instead of becoming plain ranges, so e.g. `[\\u2000-\\u0001]` does **not** raise \"invalid character class range\". This forced the row-511 span generator to use base `0x2001` step 4 (low byte ≡ 1 mod 4 avoids 0x00 and all of `DSWdsw`); the quirk itself is now asserted identical in both libraries."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: ab2546e23670cb062 (use SendMessage with to: 'ab2546e23670cb062', summary: '<5-10 word recap>' to continue this agent)\n<usage>subagent_tokens: 203427\ntool_uses: 75\nduration_ms: 1231147</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2be16944-0c16-4bac-97a9-ffb5f1a29386","uuid":"444a7d87-8b9e-4554-bd80-e4682bee7efa","timestamp":"2026-09-04T05:21:26.183Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"You are writing DIFFER