row(rc) <message>\"` / `\"ok <repr>\"`, so it\n  compares exact error class + message text. `flags` is 0 or `JS_STRICT`.\n- `diff_native(label, act, flags)` where `act: fn(&Api, JS)` drives the raw C API\n  inside a js_pcall (so throws are caught, not fatal). Use `emit(&str)` inside the\n  action to record observations; parameters come from `set_pi/pi/pic`, `set_ps/ps`,\n  `set_pf/pf` (thread-local, set before the call).\n- `repr_at(a, J, idx)` / `str_at(a, J, idx)` for NON-destructive observation\n  (`js_torepr`/`js_tostring` overwrite the stack slot in place — never observe with\n  the raw calls).\n- `Api` has a field for every exported symbol (e.g. `(a.js_ploadstring)(J, name, src)`).\n- `Rng::new(seed)` for reproducible randomized inputs: `.below(n)`, `.range_i64(a,b)`,\n  `.f64()`, `.string(maxlen)`.\n- `libs()` returns `&Pair { c: Api, r: Api }` if you need both explicitly, plus\n  `same(label, c_out, r_out)` to compare.\n\nTEST CONTENT — one test fn per group of ERRORS.md rows, covering EVERY row 1..169:\n- All `jsY_error` messages from jslex.c: unterminated string/comment/regexp, bad\n  escapes (`\\x`, `\\u`, octal in strict), malformed number, number with letter\n  suffix, unexpected character, identifier escapes, JSON lexer errors, ...\n- All 44 `jsP_expect` sites and 7 `jsP_error` sites from jsparse.c: every \"unexpected\n  token: X (expected Y)\" shape, plus `JS_ASTLIMIT` (400 nested expressions) — build\n  the deep-nesting source programmatically.\n- All 28 `jsC_error` sites and both `js_evalerror` sites from jscompile.c: duplicate\n  parameter/variable in strict mode, invalid assignment target, `delete` of an\n  unqualified name in strict mode, `with` in strict mode, bad `continue`/`break`\n  label, `return` outside a function, invalid use of `eval`, redefining\n  `arguments`/`eval`, getter/setter arity, `const` reassignment, etc.\n- Both flags (0 and JS_STRICT) for every source, since `J->strict` gates many rows.\n- Sentinel-return rows (e.g. `jsY_tokenstring` out of range, `jsY_findword` miss) are\n  called directly through the `Api` fields.\n- Add randomized fuzzing: a test that generates several thousand random token\n  soups / random unicode source strings (fixed seed) and asserts the two libraries\n  return the identical accept/reject result and identical message.\n\nUse plain source strings, NOT `js_pushliteral` or `js_newcfunction` with temporary\nCString names — the C stores those pointers without copying.\n\nWORKFLOW\n1. Write the file.\n2. `cd translation && timeout 600 cargo test --release --offline --test phase_c_syntax -- --test-threads=1`\n   (always use --offline; the network is unavailable).\n3. Iterate until it compiles and runs.\n4. If a test reveals a GENUINE divergence between the C and the Rust `.so`\n   (identical input, different output), do NOT try to fix translation/src — instead\n   mark that one test `#[ignore = \"DIVERGENCE: ...\"]` with a precise comment and\n   keep going. Make sure the file ends with all non-ignored tests PASSING.\n5. Write the list of ERRORS.md row numbers you covered to\n   `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-oXxm9Q/tmpwk/covered_syntax.txt`\n   (one line per row: `<row> <test fn name>`).\n\nFINAL REPORT: number of test fns, number of ERRORS.md rows covered, and the FULL\ndetail of every divergence found (input source, C output, Rust output).","agentId":"afe4bf6b970052834","agentType":"general-purpose","harnessNoteCount":0,"harnessTailCount":0,"harnessSectionHash":"0ef30bf95ea195f1","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done.\n\n## Result\n\n**File created:** `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-oXxm9Q/translation/tests/phase_c_syntax.rs` (only file written, plus the coverage list at `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-oXxm9Q/tmpwk/covered_syntax.txt`).\n\n**44 test fns** — 39 row-coverage tests + 5 randomized fuzz tests.\n**169 of 169 ERRORS.md rows covered** (rows 1..169), all mapped one-per-line in `covered_syntax.txt`.\n\n```