e harness.\n\nHARNESS (read `translation/tests/common/mod.rs` for the full list). Start with:\n    #![allow(non_snake_case)]\n    mod common;\n    use common::*;\nAvailable:\n- `diff_eval(label, src, flags)` — runs `src` in BOTH libraries and compares the\n  rendering `\"load-error(rc) msg\"` / `\"throw(rc) msg\"` / `\"ok <repr>\"` byte for byte.\n  `flags` is 0 or `JS_STRICT`. This is your main tool.\n- `diff_native(label, act, flags)`, `emit()`, `set_pi/pi/pic`, `set_ps/ps`,\n  `set_pf/pf` when you need the raw API.\n- `repr_at(a, J, idx)` / `str_at(a, J, idx)` for NON-destructive observation.\n- `Rng::new(seed)` with `.below/.range_i64/.f64/.string` for reproducible randomized\n  inputs; `same()`, `libs()`, `capture_stdout()`, `mask_ptrs()`.\n\nREQUIREMENTS\n- PROPERTY-STYLE: for every area, do not stop at one hand-picked value. Generate\n  MANY randomized inputs from a FIXED seed and format them into the JS source, e.g.\n  a few thousand random doubles through `String(x)`, `x.toFixed(k)`,\n  `x.toString(radix)`, `JSON.stringify(x)`, `parseFloat/parseInt`; random strings\n  through the full String method surface; random arrays through sort/join/slice/\n  splice/indexOf/concat/reverse; random dates through every Date getter.\n- Escape the generated values into the JS source carefully (or push them with the\n  raw API) so that the SAME bytes reach both libraries.\n- Run each area under both `flags = 0` and `flags = JS_STRICT`.\n- Keep the total runtime under about 3 minutes: prefer many small evals batched into\n  one script (build a script that loops over an array of inputs and joins the\n  results into one string) over one eval per input.\n\nDo NOT drive an error out of a `js_pcall` (that aborts the process): `diff_eval` and\n`diff_native` are always safe. Do NOT use `diff_isolated`/`isolated_child`.\n\nWORKFLOW\n1. Write the file.\n2. `cd translation && timeout 600 cargo test --release --offline --test phase_b_script -- --test-threads=1`\n   (always `--offline`).\n3. Iterate until it compiles and runs.\n4. If a test reveals a GENUINE divergence between the C and Rust `.so`, do NOT touch\n   translation/src — mark that test `#[ignore = \"DIVERGENCE: ...\"]` with a precise\n   comment and continue. The file must end with all non-ignored tests PASSING.\n5. Write the CONFIGS.md row numbers you covered to `tmpwk/covered_script.txt`\n   (`<row> <test fn>`).\n\nFINAL REPORT: number of test fns, CONFIGS.md rows covered, and FULL detail of every\ndivergence found (exact JS source, C output, Rust output).","agentId":"ad3b8ccf0d0d713ae","agentType":"general-purpose","harnessNoteCount":0,"harnessTailCount":0,"harnessSectionHash":"71e1d1ac8fb83aeb","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Final state: 35 tests, all passing, no `#[ignore]` needed.\n\n## What was created\n\n`/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-oXxm9Q/translation/tests/phase_b_script.rs` — 2297 lines, **35 test functions**, runs in **~46 s** (`cargo test --release --offline --test phase_b_script -- --test-threads=1`). Nothing else was modified; the full suite (`phase_b_api`, `phase_b_lowlevel`, `smoke`, and the phase_c files other agents are adding) still passes.\n\n### Harness design\n- `mk_script(inputs, exprs)` builds one script that loops `inputs × exprs`, wrapping every input in a **thunk** (`function(){return (INPUT)}`) so mutating methods (`sort`, `splice`, `length=`) get a fresh object per case, and joining all results into one string — a few thousand cases per `js_newstate`.\n- `diff_batch` compares the batch; **on divergence it re-runs every single (input, expr) pair** and panics with the minimal reproducer.\n- Self-check guards: `diff_batch`/`diff_ok`/`diff_each` assert the C side actually ran (`ok …`, not `load-error`), with a 3-entry allowlist for deliberately unparseable sources. These guards caught three of my own generator bugs (a truncated `\".\"` literal, duplicate object-literal keys emitted by the random JSON generator — mujs rejects those at compile time — and a missing `}`), which would otherwise have silently \"passed\" as identical SyntaxErrors in both libraries.\n- Inputs are escaped so identical bytes reach both libraries: `jstr` emits ≥0x80 raw as UTF-8 and only `\\uXXXX`-escapes C0/DEL; `jsnum` emits `{:e}` decimal text (`(NaN)`, `(Infinity)`, `(-0)` specials).\n- `tz_init()` pins `TZ=America/New_York` and forces both libraries to populate their cached `LocalTZA()` under the same TZ before any Date expression, and asserts they agree.\n\n### Volume (fixed seed `0x5EED_0B_5C_71_9701`)\n~4200 random doubles × 14 stringifiers; ~1000 boundary doubles (every decimal exponent −323..308, every 7th binary exponent, grisu2 branch boundaries) × 33 formatters; `toFixed` 0..20, `toExponential` 0..20, `toPrecision` 1..21 plus every out-of-range value; `toString` radix 2..36 plus 0/1/37/−1/fractional; ~2600 sequential code points swept through `toUpperCase`/`toLowerCase` plus 400 random astral strings; 700 random dates × 25 getters and 100 dates × 117 local/UTC setter forms; all 8 regexp flag combinations × ~500 pattern/haystack pairs × exec/test/lastIndex/match/replace/split/search; ~800 randomized JSON values × every indent shape and replacer form. Every area runs under both `flags = 0` and `flags = JS_STRICT`.\n\n### CONFIGS.md rows covered\nWritten to `tmpwk/covered_script.txt`: **14, 15, 16, 17, 18, 20, 22, 23, 35, 36, 37, 39, 41, 44, 45, 46, 48, 49–60, 75–80, 82–96, 98–115, 124, 125, 126, 143, 152–156, 160, 161, 167, 168, 171, 172, 174, 176, 177, 178–194.**\n\nNot reachable from this file: **rows 173 and 175**. `LocalTZA()` is cached in a function-local `static once` per library, so exactly one timezone can be exercised per test process. This file pins the row-174 zone (negative offset, DST-observing) and compares every local getter/setter against its UTC twin; `TZ=UTC` (173) and `TZ=Asia/Kolkata` (175) require a separate process. This is documented in the coverage file.\n\n### Divergences found\n**None.** Every one of the ~500,000 JS-level observations agrees byte for byte between `c_src/build/libmujs.so` and `translation/target/release/libmujs.so`, including all number formatting (grisu2, `toFixed`/`toExponential`/`toPrecision`, radix 2..36), full-Unicode case mapping, `reprstr` vs `fmtstr` escaping, sparse-array resize ordering, every regexp flag combination, and every Date getter/setter/format. No test needed `#[ignore]`."}],"resolvedModel":"global.anthropic.claude-opus-5[1m]","totalDurationMs":1710666,"totalTokens":194977,"totalToolUseCount":51,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":432,"cache_read_input_tokens":192598,"output_tokens":1945,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":383},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":432},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":4,"searchCount":0,"bashCount":41,"editFileCount":6,"linesAdded":2106,"linesRemoved":18,"otherToolCount":0}}}
