{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"a4a00c6ee92edae35","tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01FqLgu3rFhCxemNG91kaU9i","status":"completed","output_file":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-agent-jBvmJB/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-work-oXxm9Q/2be16944-0c16-4bac-97a9-ffb5f1a29386/tasks/a4a00c6ee92edae35.output","summary":"## Result\n\n`translation/tests/phase_c_runtime.rs` (3.1k lines, **47 test functions, 47 passing, 0 ignored, no divergences found**). Full workspace suite still green (`29+11+35+23+2+41+47` tests). Only that one file was created; nothing else touched. Row map written to `tmpwk/covered_runtime.txt`.\n\n### Coverage: 154 of rows 170–338\n\nGrouped tests: stack underflow (`js_pop`/`js_remove`/`js_replace`/`js_insert`), `js_rot*` counts in-frame, `stackidx` out-of-range masking, `CHECKSTACK` overflow for all 16 pushing primitives, JS/lightweight recursion limits, JS_TRYLIMIT via nested `try`, all `js_ptry`/`js_try*` entry points with a full try stack, readonly/dontconf paths of `jsR_setproperty`/`jsR_defproperty`/`jsR_delproperty` in both modes (plain, array `length`, String `length`/indices, RegExp slots, getter-only, DONTCONF, transient, non-extensible/sealed/frozen), array-length limits, `js_setlimit` run/mem, allocator-failure `js_newstate`, all 7 variadic throwers + all 7 `js_new*error` constructors, 256-byte message truncation, `js_toobject`/`jsV_toobject`, `js_toregexp`/`js_touserdata`/`jsR_tofunction`, call/construct/eval errors, `js_instanceof`, referenceerror paths, out-of-range FFI enums (state flags, attribute words, regexp flags, `jsV_newobject` classes, `toprimitive` hints), NULL-pointer arguments, and 600 randomized (recv, op, name/index, value, atts) tuples × 2 flag sets.\n\nTo make the suite provably non-vacuous I pinned the **C ground-truth message text** for every reachable thrower: `ground_truth_messages_js` (36 sources) and `ground_truth_messages_native` (20 C-API modes) assert the exact C string in addition to C-vs-Rust equality; the same is done inline for `stack underflow!`, `stack error!`, `not implemented yet`, `stack overflow`, `call stack overflow`, `exception stack overflow`, `invalid string length`, `'ro' is read-only`.\n\nTwo exports needed for the task (`js_error` … `js_urierror`) are variadic and absent from `Api`, so they are fetched by name from the *same two `.so` paths* via `common::c_so()`/`rust_so()` (dlopen returns the identical handle) — still only `.so` exports, no Rust functions called directly.\n\n### Rows not covered (15) and why\n- **213, 214, 216, 319, 281, 282** — `assert()` → `abort()`. The C build has no `NDEBUG`, so these are process-fatal by design.\n- **210** — the `jsR_unflattenarray` handler sets `obj->properties = NULL`; the *next* gc or `js_freestate` then does `obj->properties->level` → NULL deref in both libraries. Not observable non-fatally.\n- **215** — needs `flat_length == JS_ARRAYLIMIT` (a 1 GiB flat array).\n- **245** — unreachable: `jsR_pushtrace`'s JS_ENVLIMIT guard always fires before `jsR_savescope`'s (`savescope` has no caller that is not preceded by `pushtrace`).\n- **249** — defensive dead branch, no input reaches it.\n- **258, 259, 280** — `js_endtry` underflow / `js_throw` without a try / default panic: all end in `abort()`; already covered by `phase_c_isolated.rs`.\n- **334** — `100*gtot/ntot` with `ntot == 0` is a SIGFPE, and a bootstrapped state always has objects.\n- **335** — the gc report is a fixed-width format that can never exceed the 255-byte buffer.\n\n### Divergences found: **none**\nBoth libraries matched byte-for-byte everywhere, including exact `js_gc` report counts (`0/1 envs, 1/1 funs, 1/740 objs, 0/1495 props`), the *exact allocation-call count* during bootstrap (budgeted allocator flips `js_newstate` from NULL to non-NULL at the same budget), the JS_TRYLIMIT flip point (n=62 for C-level `js_savetry`, n=64 for script-level `try`), and the unspecified argument-evaluation order inside `js_setproperty`.\n\n### Ground-truth notes (C behaviour that contradicts ERRORS.md / the task brief)\n1. **Rows 227/228 are unreachable from JS source.** `OP_SETPROP` does `obj = js_toobject(J,-3); transient = !js_isobject(J,-3);` — `jsV_toobject` rewrites the stack slot to an object *in place*, so `transient` is always 0. `'use strict'; 'abc'.foo=1` yields `ok 1`, not a TypeError. The message is only reachable through the C API `js_setproperty`, where `transient` is computed from the untouched slot (covered as `ground_truth_messages_native` mode 12).\n2. **Row 241's example is wrong.** `Math` is only `JS_DONTENUM`, so `delete Math` → `true`. The `JS_DONTCONF` globals are `NaN`/`Infinity`/`undefined`; the test uses those.\n3. **Row 244's strict branch is unreachable** — `delete <identifier>` is a strict-mode SyntaxError, so `js_delvar`'s strict TypeError cannot be triggered from JS and there is no C entry point.\n4. Actual messages differ from the brief: runlimit is **\"script ran too long\"** (not \"excessive CPU usage\"); JS_ENVLIMIT is **\"call stack overflow\"** / **\"stack overflow\"** (**\"too much recursion\"** is JS_ASTLIMIT in `jsparse.c`, i.e. rows 1–169).\n5. `js_pushlstring` checks only `n > JS_STRLIMIT`; any `n` between the real buffer length and `1<<28`, or a negative `n`, drives an out-of-bounds copy in both libraries (initially SIGSEGV'd my test) — documented in the test and excluded.\n6. `js_gc`'s report goes through `J->report` (default: **stderr**), never fd 1; the test installs a report callback so the text is diffed.\n7. `js_newuserdata` stores the tag **pointer** without copying — a temporary `CString` tag makes `js_touserdata` read freed memory (it silently matched a later `\"Bar\"` allocation during development). All tags in the file are `static` byte strings.","usage":{"total_tokens":262331,"tool_uses":111,"duration_ms":1861496},"uuid":"89b7b6c0-8cab-4bce-a6a4-768fed5537e7","session_id":"2be16944-0c16-4bac-97a9-ffb5f1a29386"}
