tween the libraries: wrap such output in `mask_ptrs()`.\n- `js_gc(J, 1)` report counts are identical, but if you compare allocator byte counts,\n  strip digits.\n- Rows 173/175 need a different `TZ` than the rest of the process; a test process can\n  only initialise `LocalTZA()` once, so if you cover them, do it by running the\n  timezone-dependent Date comparison FIRST in a dedicated test fn and document the\n  limitation in a comment instead of fighting it.\n\nWORKFLOW\n1. Read CONFIGS.md rows and the existing tests; write the new file.\n2. `cd translation && timeout 600 cargo test --release --offline --test phase_b_configs -- --test-threads=1`\n   (always `--offline`). Iterate until it compiles and passes.\n3. Re-run the neighbouring suites to be sure you broke nothing:\n   `timeout 900 cargo test --release --offline -- --test-threads=1`\n4. If a test reveals a GENUINE divergence between the C and Rust `.so`, do NOT touch\n   translation/src — mark that test `#[ignore = \"DIVERGENCE: ...\"]` with a precise\n   comment and report it. All non-ignored tests must PASS.\n5. Edit `translation/CONFIGS.md`: for each of the 92 rows, replace the trailing\n   `| [ ] |` with `| [x] <testfile>::<test fn> |`. Keep the table format intact and\n   do not alter the existing `[x] phase_b_script::...` entries or any row text.\n\nFINAL REPORT: for each of the 92 rows, which test covers it (existing or new); the\nnumber of new test fns; and FULL detail of any divergence found."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":743,"cache_read_input_tokens":260688,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":743,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":17,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2be16944-0c16-4bac-97a9-ffb5f1a29386","uuid":"15c49886-bb16-442f-9600-d434da30d0aa","timestamp":"2026-09-04T05:34:32.308Z"}
