{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"af33cc97b99e9a75b","tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01Y9hKnfBpBoYWrvrFodjeAa","status":"completed","output_file":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-agent-jBvmJB/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-work-oXxm9Q/2be16944-0c16-4bac-97a9-ffb5f1a29386/tasks/af33cc97b99e9a75b.output","summary":"Done. All 195 rows of `CONFIGS.md` are now ticked, all suites pass, and no divergence was found.\n\n## (A) Rows already covered by existing tests — 21 of the 92\n\n| rows | existing test |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | `phase_b_api::state_flags_context_atpanic_report` (default allocator, `flags=0`, `js_freestate`) |\n| 6, 7 | `phase_c_runtime::r283_r285_newstate_allocator_failures` (null_alloc = row 6; budget 1 = the stack allocation of row 7) |\n| 43 | `phase_c_runtime::ffi_attribute_values_out_of_range` (atts 8/9/15/16/255/-1/-8/MAX/MIN through defproperty+defaccessor+defglobal) |\n| 47 | `phase_c_runtime::r193_r196_toregexp_touserdata_tofunction` mode 10 (null/null accessor) |\n| 81 | `phase_c_runtime::r311_r318_property_lookups_and_iterators` (+ `ground_truth_messages_native` mode 4 \"not an iterator\") |\n| 131, 136 | `phase_c_runtime::r269_r278_ptry_with_full_try_stack` (`js_ptry` refusal without longjmp; `js_dostring` ok/bad/throw with report) |\n| 133, 135 | `phase_c_runtime::r247_r255_call_construct_errors` |\n| 139 | `phase_c_isolated::all_isolated_cases_match` (case `endtry_underflow`) |\n| 140 | `phase_c_runtime::r257_savetry_overflow_caught_by_js_catch` |\n| 141 | `phase_c_runtime::r171_checkstack_overflow_every_push` (+ `r245_r246_deep_recursion_limits`) |\n| 142 | `phase_c_runtime::r197_js_pop_underflow` |\n| 144 | `phase_c_runtime::r325_r331_variadic_throwers` |\n| 145, 150 | `phase_c_runtime::r204_rot_counts_in_frame` |\n| 146 | `phase_c_runtime::r199_js_insert_not_implemented` |\n| 147, 148 | `phase_c_runtime::r198_r200_remove_replace_stack_error` |\n| 149 | `phase_c_runtime::r192_r298_stackidx_out_of_range` |\n\nTwo rows I first assumed were covered turned out **not** to be: rows 69/73 — `phase_c_runtime` op 6 builds `js_newcfunctionx` *before* `js_newuserdatax`, so under a small memlimit the cfunction throws first and the userdata call is never reached (verified by transcript). They are now covered by a new test.\n\n## (B) New file `translation/tests/phase_b_configs.rs` — 29 test fns, 71 rows\n\n`state_flag_words_and_dostring_strictness` (2-5, 9-flag sweep incl. 0xFFFFFFFE/0x80000000/0x40000000) · `state_context_report_and_panic_handlers` (9,10,11) · `newstate_allocator_budget_and_actx` (8, actx checked on every alloc/free) · `compile_strict_rejections_and_acceptance` (12,13) · `readonly_and_transient_writes` (19,21) · `try_frame_restores_state` (24,138) · `setlimit_every_shape` (25-33) · `attribute_words_and_accumulation` (34,38,40,42) · `userdata_callback_matrix` (61,62,64-68; 16 callback masks × 3 prototypes) · `newuserdatax_out_of_memory_finalizer` (69,73) · `cfunction_shapes_lengths_and_finalizers` (70,71,72,74; 6 kinds × 3 lengths × 4 arg counts × call/construct) · `pushliteral_pointer_identity` (97) · `gc_report_and_implicit_collection` (116,117,118) · `refs_and_registry_names` (119-122) · `dumpstrings_fresh_and_populated` (123) · `torepr_index_semantics_and_tryrepr` (127,128) · `ploadstring_filename_and_error_shapes` (129,130) · `pcall_and_pconstruct_success` (132,134) · `loadstring_versus_eval_strictness_and_scope` (137) · `currentfunction_and_pushglobal_identity` (151) · `predicates_over_every_value_shape` (157,158,159) · `try_conversion_defaults` (162-165) · `touserdata_and_toobject_autoboxing` (166) · `defproperty_throw_flag_and_delglobal` (169) · `newobjectx_prototype_variants` (170) · `freestate_teardown_and_finalizers` (63,195) · `a1_date_timezone_utc_first` (173) · `a2_date_timezone_half_hour_offset_child` + `zz_date_timezone_from_env` (175).\n\nProperty-style randomization from fixed seeds: 250 random attribute triples/names, 200 random `(runlimit, memlimit)` × workload pairs, 300 random receiver/name/index/value writes, 250 random registry names/value kinds, 120 random/fuzzed `js_ploadstring` sources, 40 random Date epochs per timezone, 40 random report messages, random `js_try*` defaults. Every test also has ground-truth assertions on the C side (\"script ran too long\", \"out of memory\", \"transient object\", `badctx=0`, `post ud=1 cf=1`, descriptor bit patterns, `same_ptr=true`, argument padding `1+max(len,nargs)`, `_Undefined`/`_Null`/`_True`/`_False`, …) so no test can silently pass while exercising nothing.\n\n**Divergences found: none.** All non-ignored, zero `#[ignore]`.\n\nThree C-level facts worth recording (identical in both libraries, documented in comments rather than tested as divergences):\n- **NULL `filename` to `js_ploadstring` is UB**: `jsC_compilescript` does `F->filename = js_intern(J, J->filename)` and `jsS_insert` `strcmp`s it → identical SIGSEGV in both `.so`s. Row 129's \"filename NULL\" variant was replaced with `\"\"`/two other names.\n- Row 12's list is approximate: `var eval` / `function f(eval){}` / `eval = 1` / `function eval(){}` raise an **EvalError even non-strict**, `010` is rejected unconditionally, and an octal *escape* (`'\\012'`) is accepted even in strict mode. Encoded in the test table.\n- `js_getlength` autoboxes its slot (`js_getproperty` → `js_toobject` in place), and `js_trystring`/`js_tryrepr` convert in place — so row 97/162-165 observations are taken on copies.\n\nTimezone limitation (as instructed): `LocalTZA()` caches in a function-local `static` per library, so one process sees one zone. Row 173 (`TZ=UTC`) runs first in this binary (name sorts first, `--test-threads=1`), and row 175 (`TZ=Asia/Kolkata`, verified `getTimezoneOffset() == -330`) runs in a re-exec of the same test binary — using a private `Command` spawn, not the `diff_isolated`/`isolated_child` harness.\n\nVerification: `cargo test --release --offline -- --test-threads=1` → 265 tests, 0 failures (`phase_b_configs`: 29 passed in ~1 s); the new file compiles warning-free.","usage":{"total_tokens":410785,"tool_uses":168,"duration_ms":2918542},"uuid":"b7fd0e3e-0e40-419d-b75c-743744ea4a88","session_id":"2be16944-0c16-4bac-97a9-ffb5f1a29386"}
